  },
  "findings": [
    "All seven M255 placements emit four ZIP1 sites using current sum v0 as high-byte filler, four GP-to-SIMD FMOV sites, and four subsequent USHLL/AND/UADALP sequences. All corresponding M4095 placements lack ZIP1 and GP-to-SIMD FMOV and widen directly from vector D loads. All fourteen bodies are stack-free and call-free.",
    "M255 planes main loop 0x619c0..0x61a38 consumes16 ranks in31 instructions; M4095 0xc1dc0..0xc1e08 consumes16 ranks in19 instructions. This loop comparison is semantically normalized, unlike whole-body static instruction counts.",
    "The compiler ZIP1 result interleaves four loaded bytes with live accumulator bytes; USHLL widens pairs and AND0x000000ff-per-u32 discards the accumulator bytes. Correctness is preserved, but the emitted path introduces v0(previous)->ZIP1->USHLL->AND->UADALP->v0(next) four times. Thus widening cannot issue independently of the preceding reduction. M4095 only couples the later UADALP update to v0.",
    "This identifies avoidable load-bridge/reduction coupling independent of placement, not an inherent byte-layout cost and not a measured-cycle attribution. No latency/model ratio or architectural cache cause claimed."
  ],
  "source_spelling": "contiguous<u8>: vcreate_u8(load<uint32_t>(p)), vmovl_u8, low vmovl_u16; contiguous<u16>: vmovl_u16(vld1_u16(p)).",
  "control_recommendation": [
    "A vld1_dup_u32/reinterpret spelling may remove GP transfer but must be checked for the same dead-fill ZIP1 dependence.",
    "A full16-byte ordered vector load followed by all four widened subpackets preserves every input byte, reducing optimizer freedom to synthesize masked irrelevant filler. Require actual emitted review and matched consumer/oracle before attributing performance."
  ],
